{#
  The insertion buttons for one automatic e-mail's declared variables
  (Core\Mail\Template\EmailTemplate, ARCHITECTURE.md §8.7bis).

  With `target` set, a click inserts `{{ '{{ nom }}' }}` at the cursor of
  that input — the subject field. With `target` null, a click copies the
  placeholder to the clipboard instead: the body is edited inside the
  shared rich-text modal, which is not on screen when these buttons are,
  and a button that silently did nothing would be worse than one that
  says what it did.

  Each button shows the French label; the placeholder itself and the
  example value are in the tooltip, so the row reads as prose rather than
  as a wall of braces.

  Usage:
  {% include 'partials/email_variable_buttons.html.twig' with {
      variables: template.variables,
      target: 'email-subject',   -- or null
  } only %}
#}
{% if variables is not empty %}
    <div class="d-flex flex-wrap gap-2 email-variable-buttons"
         {% if target %}data-target="{{ target }}"{% endif %}>
        {% for variable in variables %}
            <button type="button" class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-secondary"
                    data-variable="{{ variable.name }}"
                    title="{{ '{{ ' ~ variable.name ~ ' }}' }} — exemple : {{ variable.example }}">
                {{ variable.label }}
            </button>
        {% endfor %}
    </div>
{% else %}
    <p class="small text-body-secondary mb-0">Cet email ne prend aucune variable.</p>
{% endif %}
